WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.454
In the year 1689, the Qing dynasty negotiated with Russia.

00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:06.931
They needed to resolve the border issue in the north.

00:00:07.558 --> 00:00:10.612
Songgotu knelt to receive the imperial edict, his expression very solemn.

00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:13.015
The Kangxi Emperor sent Songgotu on a long journey to Nerchinsk.

00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:18.293
The delegation traveled a very long way on horseback and by carriage.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.380
Along the way they passed through grasslands and also through great forests.

00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:26.251
The Russian delegation crossed a great river and came to the camp to meet.

00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:29.323
Both sides sat inside a large tent and discussed patiently.

00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:31.462
A map was spread out on the table, and everyone pointed and discussed.

00:00:31.462 --> 00:00:35.214
The negotiations lasted many days, and the atmosphere was peaceful.

00:00:35.214 --> 00:00:38.767
The two sides sometimes argued, but their tone remained polite.

00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:41.176
In the end, the two countries signed the Treaty of Nerchinsk.

00:00:41.176 --> 00:00:45.452
The border was clearly drawn, and trade could also be carried out.

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:47.739
The people outside the tents all showed smiles.

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:50.427
This was a major event in the diplomatic history of the Qing dynasty.

00:00:51.046 --> 00:00:53.654
Using negotiation instead of quarreling brought peace.

00:00:53.654 --> 00:00:56.756
From then on, the peoples of the two countries interacted in friendship.
